  "answer": "This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#33 is the main tracking issue for a context menu editor, and the others were closed as duplicates of it. PowerToys#45905 asks for the same thing as your ticket: choosing which items appear in the compact Explorer menu. That one was closed as a duplicate of #33. PowerToys doesn't offer this yet, and the archive shows no planned release. Add your Word, Notepad and 'create desktop shortcut' examples as a comment on #33 and give it a thumbs-up. In the meantime, the discussion in #33 suggests third-party tools such as NileSoft Shell, which can remove existing entries. Another option is the registry-based switch to the classic menu, but that needs a registry edit and brings back the full menu."
